      "body": "in f805f095fd8c8e2b4b7a46490069b5dfa8751586 test: Replace hardcoded extended keys with ExtendedKey helpers\n\nIf I am not wrong this can cause some problems when running the test framework with `--randomseed=`. As same seed could produce different results, making errors non reproducible. This is because the seed is not applied into the rng before you call a function.\n\nA solution to this would be to not use an rng for this test and hardcode some value.\nFor example:\n```diff\n$ git diff\ndiff --git a/test/functional/wallet_miniscript.py b/test/functional/wallet_miniscript.py\nindex 6daf21b9b3..a6d9cb6843 100755\n--- a/test/functional/wallet_miniscript.py\n+++ b/test/functional/wallet_miniscript.py\n@@ -10,9 +10,8 @@ from test_framework.psbt import PSBT, PSBT_IN_SHA256\n from test_framework.test_framework import BitcoinTestFramework\n from test_framework.util import assert_equal\n \n\n-TPRVS = [ExtendedPrivateKey.generate().to_string() for _ in range(0, 3)]\n-TPUBS = [ExtendedPrivateKey.generate().pubkey().to_string() for _ in range(0, 7)]\n+TPRVS = [ExtendedPrivateKey.from_seed(f\"miniscript-private-{i}\".encode()).to_string() for i in range(3)]\n+TPUBS = [ExtendedPrivateKey.from_seed(f\"miniscript-public-{i}\".encode()).pubkey().to_string() for i in range(7)]\n PUBKEYS = [\n     \"02aebf2d10b040eb936a6f02f44ee82f8b34f5c1ccb20ff3949c2b28206b7c1068\",\n     \"030f64b922aee2fd597f104bc6cb3b670f1ca2c6c49b1071a1a6c010575d94fe5a\",\n\n```",
